Subject: [PATCH] psu: treat cancelled polling timers as normal lifecycle events

Cancelling the wait timer while destroying or replacing a sensor reports
operation_aborted. This is not a failed PSU read or scheduling failure.
Log it at debug level and retain the existing early return.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/psu/PSUSensor.cpp
+++ b/src/psu/PSUSensor.cpp
@@ -181,7 +181,8 @@
     waitTimer.async_wait([weakRef](const boost::system::error_code& ec) {
         if (ec == boost::asio::error::operation_aborted)
         {
-            lg2::error("Failed to reschedule");
+            // Timer cancellation is expected when replacing a sensor.
+            lg2::debug("PSU sensor polling timer cancelled");
             return;
         }
         std::shared_ptr<PSUSensor> self = weakRef.lock();
